<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Standard Bank unit loses director.</title>
<headline>Standard Bank unit loses director.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Standard Bank Ltd said on Wednesday that Graeme Stephens, director of corporate finance at its Standard Corporate and Merchant Bank unit, has left the firm.</p>
<p>Stephens, along with Standard corporate finance staff Shaun Rosenthal and David Lake, is to join investment firm Capital Alliance (Captall).</p>
<p>Captall heads up a black empowerment consortium which last year agreed to buy Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd's 34.9 percent holding in JCI Ltd for 2.88 billion rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
